This PR first implements the support on the trino connector side for integrating the pixels `vector` type as the underlying data source for trino `array(double)`.

This PR then implements distributed Exact Nearest Neighbour search as an aggregation function `exact_nns_agg(arr_col, inputVec, distFunc, k)` that can be invoked in trino, utilising multi-node cluster. `arr_col` is the array column, input vec is the vector for which we want to find the nearest neighbors, distFunc can be euclidean distance, dot product and cosine similarity, and `k` is to specify that we want the top k neighbors.  

This PR also implements three different types of distance calculation as trino udfs: euclidean distance, dot product and cosine similarity that can be called on comparing distance on two vectors;

